{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "isolation_regret_v2",
  "intent": "Add an isolation ratio term (1 - nearest_remaining/mean_remaining), weighted by (1-progress), to prioritize spatially isolated candidates early in the tour. This directly targets uniform instances, where the parent's cluster-density term is rank-preserving and its 0.053 family loss suggests greedy nearest choices still create long detours to sparse outliers. Isolation early means these outliers are absorbed before they become expensive returns. Modestly boost the late return coefficient (0.40->0.45) for stronger closure and slow regret decay (0.20->0.15) so look-ahead persists into midtour. Cluster-density weight is trimmed (0.06->0.05) since the new isolation term partially substitutes for its clustering signal.",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "regret"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f[\"distance\"]\n    r = f[\"return_distance\"]\n    nr = f[\"nearest_remaining\"]\n    mr = f[\"mean_remaining\"]\n    g = f[\"regret\"]\n    p = f[\"progress\"]\n    cd = f[\"cluster_density\"]\n    inv_mr = 1.0 / max(mr, 1e-9)\n    isolation = 1.0 - nr * inv_mr\n    return -d + (0.15 + 0.45 * p) * r + (0.35 - 0.15 * p) * g + 0.05 * (1 - p) * cd + 0.10 * (1 - p) * isolation",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 13,
  "reference_id": null,
  "action": "develop",
